SUMMARY:Flatlander's Folly
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nMST from Elk Pasture Gap (NC151 & 
 BRP) to Pisgah Inn\, out and back\, 7 miles\, pace about 2 mph\, less is s
 teep areas. The first part of the hike\, to Little Pisgah\, is a 1\,200 fo
 ot climb over 1.5 miles. That's the steep\, slower part. Then it's a steep
  descent to the Buck Springs Lodge site and then on to Pisgah Inn. We'll t
 ake our break at the Inn\, then return.\n\n7 miles\, 1\,200 feet of steep 
 elevation\, difficult trails\, not a dog friendly hike.\n\nParking is limi
 ted at the trailhead\; we will carpool from the French Broad River overloo
 k.\n\nWith the heat of summer\, we're hiking at higher elevations for cool
 er temperatures. This will entail longer drives and perhaps more difficult
  hikes. That's the plan. God is laughing.\n\n**Release of Liability:**\nTh
 e organizer of this trip is a volunteer and not a professional guide. The 
 function of the organizer is only to organize this trip. If you sign up or
  participate in this event you acknowledge that you freely and voluntarily
  agree to assume all risks of injuries\, illnesses\, and damages arising f
 rom\, as a result of\, and associated with this event. In addition\, you a
 cknowledge that you agree to the Meetup Terms of Service: [https://help.me
 etup.com/hc/en-us/articles/360027447252-Terms-of-Service#h_9e385395-a405-4
 361-8afc-854a4f586c82.](https://help.meetup.com/hc/en-us/articles/36002744
 7252-Terms-of-Service#h_9e385395-a405-4361-8afc-854a4f586c82.)
